{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters","id":1018550,"title":"Legalized Monsters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-17T12:36:26-08:00","id":1018550,"title":"Legalized Monsters","content":"Hi everyone! Wasn't sure where to post this since it covers various different angles, so thought I would just do it here.<br /> <br /> Has anyone every played in a world where society knows that stories they were told as children are real? What if, in one country, it became legal to be one of those monsters? I've been reading a book series where this happens. It is early in the stages so there are still a lot of issues (no voting privileges etc.). <br /> <br /> What I want to ask, is how do you think this would effect your stories if all of a sudden, the country you are in legalized this. That it would be considered murder to just kill own without a warrant. How would your hunters act? Or your monsters? What happens when the rest of worlds monsters come flocking to your country so they don't have to worry about those pesky humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:07:58-08:00","id":1018559,"title":"","content":"Well, it would mean many different things depending upon gameline you pick to legalize.<br /> <br /> Vampires, Werewolves, Sin-Eaters, and Beasts would have the easiest time being accepted as real since they can be a lot more easily recognized. They would have a hell of a time being accepted into society on the account of their diets (even Sin-Eaters, can see the religious outcry now) and predisposition as predators (The Geist will have it's day in the sun after all.)<br /> <br /> Mages, Changelings, and Demons would have a difficult time being accepted as real because of Quisience, the Mask, and Cover respectively. Although if they were accepted on some level they would probably have the most easiest time being accepted since they can be a lot more human in appetite and goals. (Unless the whole soul stealing stuff comes up for...well, hot damn, all three gamelines!)<br /> <br /> And Promethean and Mummy I cannot see happening at all on account of Disguiet and Sybaris. <br /> <br /> This scenario could lead to some interesting social Chronicles though. Might need to run one sometime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T13:29:23-08:00","id":1018566,"title":"","content":"Chapter three of the Mirrors supplement for 1ED has some suggesttions for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T14:21:22-08:00","id":1018582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters?p=1018559#post1018559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires, Werewolves, Sin-Eaters, and Beasts would have the easiest time being accepted as real since they can be a lot more easily recognized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves cause Lunacy, and most people will have Breaking Points upon witnessing the supernatural. Some will go away as the mere existence of supernaturals is within the realm of peoples possibility, but others like Lunacy or some of the more powerful abilities would still cause mental harm to people.<br /> <br /> We've had <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/490382-the-world-of-darkness-revealed-and-tumblr\">threads</a> like these. There's a book, <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/82477/World-of-Darkness-Mirrors\" target=\"_blank\">Mirrors</a>, that has a section about it. You might look to them for further ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T20:26:41-08:00","id":1018660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters?p=1018582#post1018582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Werewolves cause Lunacy, and most people will have Breaking Points upon witnessing the supernatural. Some will go away as the mere existence of supernaturals is within the realm of peoples possibility, but others like Lunacy or some of the more powerful abilities would still cause mental harm to people</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be more true in 1st Edition Forsaken, but 2nd Edition has rules and conditions for when Lunacy goes terribly wrong for the Uratha. Also, unlike Quiscience, there isn't any cosmic force that cleans up the carnage left behind from a Werewolf so I'd argue there'd still be more evidence of their existence that Mages, Changelings, and Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> P.S. Crap, how could I forget about Mirrors!? You should definitely go check that out if you're able.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Forgot about Mirrors 12-17-2016, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:30:20-08:00","id":1018684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters?p=1018660#post1018660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That might be more true in 1st Edition Forsaken, but 2nd Edition has rules and conditions for when Lunacy goes terribly wrong for the Uratha. Also, unlike Quiscience, there isn't any cosmic force that cleans up the carnage left behind from a Werewolf so I'd argue there'd still be more evidence of their existence that Mages, Changelings, and Demons.</div> </div> </div> </div>People who suffer from Lunacy forget exactly what happened unless they get an Exceptional Success. There's also the Veil ritual, which gets rid of any recordings of a supernatural activity. All in second edition. Regardless, people getting afflicted with Lunacy upon witnessing a werewolf being a werewolf would be a huge public health concern, and would not help them be accepted.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure what rules or conditions you're talking about 'for when Lunacy goes terribly wrong for the Uratha.' Not only is it a defense mechanism, it's a weapon they can inflict on people, causing them to worship the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-18-2016, 12:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:48:39-08:00","id":1018686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters?p=1018684#post1018684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> People who suffer from Lunacy forget exactly what happened unless they get an Exceptional Success. There's also the Veil ritual, which gets rid of any recordings of a supernatural activity. All in second edition. I'm not sure what rules or conditions you're talking about 'for when Lunacy goes terribly wrong for the Uratha.' Not only is it a defense mechanism, it's a weapon they can inflict on people, causing them to worship the werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm...I might be remembering Condition that make a human go all Hero over the Uratha and obsess about hunting them down or destroying them. <br /> <br /> But other than that, I still don't see your point. The fact the Uratha need a ritual to fix oopses like being filmed or caught on camera is exactly why they'd be more easily believe to exists. No werewolf, vampire, sin-eater, or beast is good enough to 100% cover their tracks all the time. If that were the case there wouldn't be any Hunters. And that's not even counting the physical evidence the Uratha leave behind: Footprints of shifting, giant claw marks, human blood patterns in impossibly large animal fights, and not to mention all the Wolf-Blooded out there who are immune to Lunacy. (And yes, Sleepers/Enchanted/Stygmatics can do the same thing for the above mentioned reality editing, but my point is that some splats just leave more physical evidence of their passing than others.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T21:55:04-08:00","id":1018688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1018550-legalized-monsters?p=1018686#post1018686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm...I might be remembering Condition that make a human go all Hero over the Uratha and obsess about hunting them down or destroying them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds more like Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But other than that, I still don't see your point. The fact the Uratha need a ritual to fix oopses like being filmed or caught on camera is exactly why they'd be more easily believe to exists. No werewolf, vampire, sin-eater, or beast is good enough to 100% cover their tracks all the time. If that were the case there wouldn't be any Hunters. And that's not even counting the physical evidence the Uratha leave behind: Footprints of shifting, giant claw marks, human blood patterns in impossibly large animal fights, and not to mention all the Wolf-Blooded out there who are immune to Lunacy. (And yes, Sleepers/Enchanted/Stygmatics can do the same thing for the above mentioned reality editing, but my point is that some splats just leave more physical evidence of their passing than others.) </div> </div> </div>If whenever a werewolf gets injured, changes form, or uses a magical ability, everyone who witnesses it suffers Lunacy, they're going to be walking, talking problems. The mere sight of a werewolf healing supernaturally fast can make someone into spirit food, or turn them into a violent berserker.<br /> <br /> It doesn't matter if they're just 'found' or they all come out with a formal announcement from ambassadors of the nine tribes. They wouldn't be easily accepted because everyone who sees evidence of it gets unhinged. Except for wolf-blooded and other supernaturals, who don't make up the population 'accepting' these werewolves to begin with.<br /> <br /> You may be placing more emphasis on people believing in werewolves than people accepting werewolves into society. Believing in them is no problem. Much of humanity in the Chronicles of Darkness already believes in the monsters out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-18-2016, 12:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-17T22:38:41-08:00","id":1018698,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a>, ooooh I think we might be arguing the same thing here. My original post was that it was easier for people to believe in those four splats but have a lot harder time accepting them (because of all the carnage and people eating/murdering.) While the other three were harder to prove but on the surface much easier to accept. I never intended to say anyone would ever accept the Uratha, your points about Lunacy are solid arguments that would need to be addressed if such a Chronicle were to be made.<br /> <br /> P.S. I could have sworn there was this one Lunacy Condition that made the target go crazy Ahab obsessed with the werewolf. I might just be remembering Beast like you said though. :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Acknowledgement 12-18-2016, 01:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-18T10:37:28-08:00","id":1018843,"title":"","content":"People don't have to react so poorly in such an universal basis just because Lunacy. Our world already have ISIS, AIDS, contagious airborne diseases, criminals, and a lot more, and mostly our societies don't just go medieval on everyone who can cause problems. That certainly can happen on some chronicles, because it is a Dark setting, and certainly some people will have prejudice to no end and with murderous intent, but on a general basis it isn't needed, or even realistic.<br /> <br /> More probable, the first thing that will happen is that a lot of distinct ideas will form about how to deal with, from the &quot;Lets All Be Happy Friends All Is Well&quot; to the &quot;Lets Burn Them&quot;, and everything in between and tangents. While this happens, monsters are likely to be regarded as normal people, expected the same rights and to obey the same laws, until society can adapt. The multiple discrepancies will be tackled by the system in a case-by-case basis, with results depending on a lot of factors. A vampire can be forbidden by law from feeding, while other is pardoned from any crime committed in the name of feeding.<br /> <br /> I think that mostly, though, normal law will keep in place, because really, most monsters are capable of following it. Vampires and Werewolves have to deal with anger issues, but we already have to deal with people with anger issues. On their daily lives, Uratha are not required to kill people, practice theft, or anything like that. Vampires can have willing donations, and don't need to harm too much. Mages have no reason to argue against ethics, except the same reasons as any researchers.<br /> <br /> Society will have to adapt, but that will be mostly creating special politics to deal with special necessities, something we already have. Some places are prone to ignore it and hunt down the monsters, but those are the same places that condemn homosexuals for the crime of being such. Special units on every service, including security services, are likely to rise just to deal with the supernatural in their context, and most likely including the monsters themselves as personnel.<br /> <br /> Also discovering the monsters is mostly a matter of such discovery beginning. With all the ways to hide oneself from others, as a species each one won't be that hard. A given vampire, werewolf, mage, changeling or whatever can hide indefinitely, but enough evidence from a given type is enough for its discovery. And probably all the answers will come from the individuals who think they can benefit more in revealing themselves.<br /> <br /> What is most likely to change with this isn't actual human society, or the lives of lone monsters, but shadow societies. They will get attention, and the expectation to conform. Members will be able to walk back to mortal institutions, now adapted for them. Most shadow societies don't demand crimes, but they don't care, either. It will change, to some degree. Most of how those groups work is based on their necessity to hide. Suddenly this will be gone. I can imagine, lets say, the Lancea et Sanctum loosing members to some regular christian denominations that accept Kindred (not that all of them will), and having to choose between either assume a more mainstream outlook, maybe finally becoming a part of the Roman Church, or a more cultist, but still acceptable, one to keep it as the Weird Religion of Vampires, keeping more of its independence in trade for loosing some faithful, or finally going completely underground, but that time in a context where it isn't expected to be underground just for being Kindred. All of this will change a lot how the Lancea works and how it interacts with vampires' society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T18:05:43-08:00","id":1019530,"title":"","content":"All interesting thoughts. I especially like monteparnas post. All the negative effects of supernatural come from mortals seeing supernatural aspects. What if a werewolf/vampire/whatever wants to pick up it's old job as a cop/cook/reporter etc? Or what about new monsters?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-19T19:39:46-08:00","id":1019571,"title":"","content":"That will be mixed, because while society as a whole tend to a middle answer, people are going to be very diverse. Who's in command? Who decides to grant employment? How clientele is likely to behave locally? Think about black people. Some people think they're just ok, some think they're dumb, some think they're disease carriers, some think they're violent criminals to the core. Some people openly have those beliefs, and some do not see what they are doing. Some are sympathetic, but sometimes sympathetic people aren't devoid of prejudice at all.<br /> <br /> I would go for very mixed scenarios all around. For some inspiration, I would watch Everybody Hates Chris and read a lot of X-Men. Not for powers or plots, but for examples of prejudiced people being themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}